This package contains Michael Johanson's implementation of a game-state 
(infoset, action, etc) counting program for large no-limit poker games,
such as the no-limit Texas hold'em games played in the
Annual Computer Poker Competition.  It contains the source code for two
programs:

 * count_nl_infosets
 * count_limit_infosets

This implementation is written in C and was tested in a Unix environment.  
It depends on the GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic Library for support
for large integers, since the counts of large no-limit games quickly
surpass the maximum size of unsigned 64-bit integers.

We have released this software under a BSD license, the details of which
can be found in the accompanying LICENSE file.

A technical report describing the algorithm and presenting the sizes of
the no-limit games played in the Annual Computer Poker Competition
can be found online at any of the following locations:

http://www.cs.ualberta.ca/~johanson/publications/poker/2013-techreport-nl-size/2013-techreport-nl-size.html
http://webdocs.cs.ualberta.ca/~games/poker/

When run, count_nl_infosets and count_limit_infosets will print out the size
of the game in betting sequences (without cards), infosets,
game states, canonical infosets, canonical infoset-actions, and so on,
for both Royal Hold'em (Ten-Ace in four suits, for a 20 card deck)
and Texas Hold'em.

Please feel free to email Michael Johanson with any questions or
comments: johanson@ualberta.ca
